module bindings.python.pyjwt_critical_extension_validation;

// PyJWT exports both the `PyJWS` class and its `decode_complete` method in
// `__all__`: the class is the JWS consumer, and the method is where a
// compact token is parsed and its verified segments returned. RFC 7515
// §4.1.11 gives the JOSE header a `crit` parameter naming extensions the
// producer declares mandatory to process, and requires a consumer to reject
// any token whose `crit` lists an extension it does not implement -- a
// token that verifies while a declared-mandatory extension goes unenforced
// reads as signed-and-valid to a relying party keying a control on that
// extension.
//
// The header is attacker-chosen JSON, so the obligation sits with the
// consumer class, and a class that nowhere reads the `crit` parameter cannot
// reject on it: the parameter must be read to be checked, and every
// implementation of the check reads that key -- wherever in the class the
// check lives. The negation therefore matches the quoted parameter read
// against the class body's text, which Python hands to every method's
// context: a read in a sibling helper, in the supported-extension table, or
// in the decode routine itself all quiet the binding, while prose that
// merely says "critical" does not. The residual is the false-negative
// direction: a `crit` read that only guards encoding quiets the binding
// while the decode path still accepts the token.
//
// The clauses answer to the declared surface and the RFC, not to one
// incident: the exported class name, the exported decode entry, and the
// parameter's quoted name. A consumer class that reads `crit` anywhere does
// not match, and neither does a decode routine on any other class.

binding unsupportedCriticalExtensionAccepted {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function"
    and node.token contains "lang=python"
    and containsAny(node.context.functionName, ["decode_complete"])
    and containsAny(node.context.className, ["PyJWS"])
    and not containsAny(node.token, ["\"crit\"", "'crit'"])
  emit issue code.UnsupportedCriticalExtensionAccepted at node
}
